Given below are two statements:
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width:500px;"><tbody><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement&nbsp;I: </strong></span></td><td style="text-align: justify;">In a dicotyledonous leaf, the adaxial epidermis general bears more stomata than the abaxial epidermis.</td></tr><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement II: </strong></span></td><td style="text-align: justify;">In a dicotyledonous leaf, the adaxially placed palisade parenchyma is made up of elongated cells, which are arranged vertically and parallel to each other.</td></tr></tbody></table>
In light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:<br>1. <strong>Statement I </strong>is True but <strong>Statement II </strong>is False<br>2. <strong>Statement I </strong>is False but <strong>Statement II </strong>is True<br>3. Both <strong>Statement I </strong>and <strong>Statement II </strong>are True<br>4. Both <strong>Statement I </strong>and <strong>Statement II </strong>are False&nbsp;
